          "id": "dynamic-array",
          "slug": "dynamic-array",
          "title": "Design Dynamic Array (Vector)",
          "difficulty": "Easy",
          "is_foundation": true,
          "time_complexity_target": "O(1) amortized append, O(1) random access",
          "space_complexity_target": "O(N)",
          "timeout_ms": 2000,
          "starter_relpath": "exercises/arrays-hashing/dynamic-array/solution.cpp",
          "test_relpath": "dsa_learn/curriculum/topics/arrays-hashing/dynamic-array/tests.cpp",
          "solution_relpath": "dsa_learn/curriculum/topics/arrays-hashing/dynamic-array/solution.cpp",
          "problem_relpath": "dsa_learn/curriculum/topics/arrays-hashing/dynamic-array/problem.md",
          "reference_url": "https://roadmap.sh/datastructures-and-algorithms",
          "hints": [
            {
              "tier": 1,
              "type": "NUDGE",
              "title": "Capacity vs Size Tracking",
              "content_markdown": "Keep track of two distinct variables: `length` (current count of stored items) and `capacity` (allocated heap buffer size). When `length == capacity`, double the capacity."
            },
            {
              "tier": 2,
              "type": "STRATEGY",
              "title": "Geometric Growth & Memory Management",
              "content_markdown": "1. Initialize with `new int[capacity]`.\n2. In `push_back`: if `length == capacity`, allocate `new int[capacity * 2]`, copy old elements over, deallocate old buffer with `delete[] data`, and point `data` to new buffer.\n3. In destructor `~DynamicArray()`: execute `delete[] data` to avoid leaks."
            },
            {
              "tier": 3,
              "type": "PSEUDOCODE",
              "title": "Class Implementation Blueprint",
              "content_markdown": "```cpp\nclass DynamicArray {\n    int* data;\n    int capacity;\n    int length;\npublic:\n    DynamicArray(int cap = 2) : capacity(cap), length(0) { data = new int[capacity]; }\n    ~DynamicArray() { delete[] data; }\n    void push_back(int n) {\n        if (length == capacity) resize();\n        data[length++] = n;\n    }\n    int pop_back() { return data[--length]; }\n    int get(int i) const { return data[i]; }\n    void set(int i, int n) { data[i] = n; }\n    int size() const { return length; }\n    int get_capacity() const { return capacity; }\n};\n```"
            }
          ]
        },
