              "content_markdown": "1. `insertHead`: allocate a new node, point its `next` to `head`, then update `head`.\n2. `insertTail`: if `!head`, set `head = node`. Otherwise traverse until `curr->next == nullptr` and link.\n3. `remove`: check `0 <= index < size`. For head removal, update `head = head->next`. For other positions, stop at `index - 1`, splice out `curr->next`, and `delete` the removed node."
            },
            {
              "tier": 3,
              "type": "PSEUDOCODE",
              "title": "Complete Class Blueprint",
              "content_markdown": "```cpp\nclass LinkedList {\n    ListNode* head;\n    int size;\npublic:\n    LinkedList() : head(nullptr), size(0) {}\n    ~LinkedList() {\n        while (head) { ListNode* t = head; head = head->next; delete t; }\n    }\n    int get(int i) const {\n        if (i < 0 || i >= size) return -1;\n        ListNode* c = head;\n        for (int k = 0; k < i; ++k) c = c->next;\n        return c->val;\n    }\n    void insertHead(int v) { ListNode* n = new ListNode(v); n->next = head; head = n; size++; }\n    void insertTail(int v) { /* traverse and link */ size++; }\n    bool remove(int i) { /* unlink and delete */ size--; return true; }\n    std::vector<int> getValues() const { /* collect into vector */ }\n};\n```"
            }
          ]
        },
